  "title": "Agents got a workshop",
  "summary": "Agents gained more tools, video gained more ways to be guided, and the growing model catalog became easier to navigate.\n\nAgents can now delegate to other agents, load tools from a hosted MCP registry, transcribe audio, search and fetch web pages, and process media with FFmpeg. Endpoint-agent registration and CLI commands make them easier to set up; a new command also connects DeepSeek Harness to Pollinations models and MCP tools.\n\nRoutes were added for Seedance 2.5, Wan 3.0, and Gemini Omni video generation. Seedance gained reference image, video, and audio URLs; Wan supports short clips from text or an image; and Gemini Omni generates video with synchronized audio. Longer media requests can rejoin an in-progress job, while video frame limits are now enforced rather than silently ignored.\n\nThe catalog gained a “Hide paid” filter, searchable access and capability filters, autocomplete, and tooltips for declared context-window and video-duration limits. Eligible models now open directly in the right Play tab. Publisher-qualified IDs already work as aliases; they are planned to become canonical on September 7 at 14:00 UTC, with existing IDs remaining aliases.\n\nNew routes include MiniMax H3, Qwen Image 3, Z-Image, and paid-only GLM-5.3 Flash. GLM-5.3 moved to a direct Fireworks route and is no longer marked paid-only; its reasoning requirement remains. Text requests gained additional controls, and model lookup by ID or alias was added.",
